;; Problem statements, one per stage of the run, written before the stage is built (docs/hickey.md,
;; "And the hammock."): the problem, the information it needs that the bot does not yet gather, what
;; can go wrong, what done means in world terms, and what the last recorded failure showed. Hand-written
;; data next to goals.edn; problems_test requires a statement for every target goal and checks every
;; source exists. Stages already built cite our own recorded failures; stages ahead cite the siblings
;; (steve, ruststeve), whose notes in brain/siblings are research drafts until re-verified.
;; Update a row when a run of that stage fails in a new way: the failure is the most valuable line here.
[{:problem/stage :wood
  :problem/goals [:wood]
  :problem/statement "Hold one log from a natural tree, starting wherever the bot lands, with only what the server has sent it."
  :problem/needs ["Which loaded blocks are logs, and which log of a trunk is at feet height."
                  "Where its own drop is, and whether a leaf covers it."
                  "Whether the landing itself is usable: not water, not inside a canopy, not buried."]
  :problem/risks ["A drop lands under the trunk, out of a 1.8-tall player's reach."
                  "A leaf at head height hides the drop and walking cannot pass it."
                  "The fixture lands the bot on a pond, in a canopy or in stone."
                  "An early FINISH aborts the break."]
  :problem/done "The server's inventory read for the bot shows any *_log."
  :problem/last-failure "Recorded in CI and replayed: collect failed :not-picked-up when the bot dug the base log from two blocks above (fixed by trunk-target), and again when a low oak leaf covered the drop (fixed by digging the blocker). Recorded live 2026-10-10 on a pickaxe run and diagnosed by folding the recording: three collects in a row failed :not-picked-up because the drop lay one block up a ledge with leaves one above head height over the ledge and over the bot, so no jump rose a full block (fixed: over a one-block step, the blocker also looks one above the head, in both columns). Open, recorded by the gym (batch wood-a2, run 5, landing 21280,18720; kept in test/recordings/wood-a2-5-fail): a log dug high in a tall trunk (y 86) was not picked up, the next targets were out of reach, and walks toward y 90 stuck until the plan failed :stuck."
  :problem/sources ["brain/bot/gotchas/drop-under-the-trunk.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/leaf-canopy-over-the-drop.md"
                    "brain/bot/tooling/harness-landing.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/early-finish-aborts.md"]}
