 {:problem/stage :water-and-lava
  :problem/issue 5
  :problem/statement "The bot cannot tell it is in water or lava: liquids are passable air to the physics, nothing tracks breath, health or death, and the planner cannot interrupt a running intent, so a bot that walks into a pond sinks, walks the bottom and drowns without noticing."
  :problem/needs ["In-water, in-lava and eye-in-water flags written by the physics step every tick (eye at y+1.62, not feet+1)"
                  "Fluid kind and level per block, from the block state ids"
                  "Estimated air, fall distance, health-zero death and the respawn packet"
                  "A bank to swim to: nearest column with air at eye height and solid support"
                  "Water and lava sightings in memory, plus water-trap facts left behind after an escape"]
  :problem/risks ["Jump in water gives almost no lift; only pressing into a bank fires the 0.3 wall impulse"
                  "Swimming in an arbitrary heading goes deeper and drowns"
                  "Head goes under mid-intent and the bot drowns inside the step"
                  "A one-tick bob to dry Y reads as escaped, then the next step shoves it back in"
                  "Roofed aquifer: every move goes up into stone while air is sideways and down"
                  "Standing beside or over lava; a lily pad lid stops the rise"]
  :problem/done "From a shore landing the bot walks into water and back out: RESULT reports :escaped true, RCON confirms no water at the feet or head cell and OnGround 1b, with at least 9 of 10 CI trials passing and zero deaths."
  :problem/last-failure "clojurecraft has never attempted this. steve: the bot dove into cave water found 23 blocks down and was hard water-trapped in a 1-wide flooded pocket, losing the run (race81/192). ruststeve: rust-race-003 drowned in a water column under solid stone, every escape move going up while air was one block west and one down."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/06-water-and-lava-survival.md"
                    "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-water-traps.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-water-escape.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-lava-safety.md"]}

